    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d37">

                <pb facs="0069" n="49" xml:id="pg49"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">700.00(S)/4–1050: Circular telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Certain Diplomatic Offices
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d37-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">priority</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-04-11T00:00:00-05:00">April 11, 1950—12
                            a. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p> Infotel. We have agreed with French and UK on schedule for May meetings three
                        FonMins<anchor n="2" xml:id="d37-f2"/> and Atlantic Pact Council. Secy will
                    arrive Paris May 7 for discussions May 8 with Schuman and will proceed May 9–10
                    with Bevin and with Bevin and Schuman May 11, 12, 13. Atlantic Pact Council will
                    meet May 15, 16, and 17 subject to confirmation by other Atlantic Pact govts.
                    Advance party will probably begin preparatory talks Apr 24 in London. Our
                    preference is to break down preparatory work into two phases: 1) first week
                    beginning Apr 24 to cover broad general subjects; and 2) second week beginning
                    May 2 to cover specific area questions such as Germany, Indo-China and Near
                    East.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d37-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d37-f1-content">
                <p>Sent to Brussels, Copenhagen, The Hague, Lisbon, Moscow, Oslo, Reykjavik, and
                    Rome.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d37-f2" n="2" xml:id="d37-f2-content">
                <p>For documentation covering preparation for the approaching meeting of the three
                    Foreign Ministers in London, together with coverage of the ministerial meetings
                    and the lower echelon preparatory talks that preceded them, see <ref
                        target="#pg828">pp. 828</ref> ff.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
